    "title": "There were 335 students enrolled in Black Hawk School District in 2024-25 school year",
    "text": "Black Hawk School District Superintendent William Chambers (2023) | Black Hawk School District\nBlack Hawk School District Superintendent William Chambers (2023) | Black Hawk School District\nWisconsin Department of Public Instruction.\nOf all the students welcomed in the 2024-25 school year, 59.7% identified themselves as boys, 40.3% as girls.\nData also shows that most of the students were white, accounting for 95.8% of the Black Hawk School District total enrollment.\nBlack Hawk School District covers three schools within Lafayette County, with its main office in South Wayne.\nAmong the three schools in the district, Black Hawk Elementary School recorded the highest enrollment of 163 students in the 2024-25 school year.\nWisconsin had a student-to-teacher ratio of 14-to-1 in 2025, lower than the national average of 16-to-1, according to Public School Review.\nSchool | Total Enrollment |\n---|---|\nBlack Hawk Elementary School | 163 |\nBlack Hawk High School | 96 |\nBlack Hawk Middle School | 76 |",
